Z||000005||Bob Englert||12-08-2000||09:38 PM||||Ken:<P>There is ALWAYS money involved  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> !<P>My daughter's 87 coupe had a bad speedometer when we bought it.  It would work for a while and then just get stuck at 62 mph.  I replaced the VSS which had no effect.  I then swapped the speedometer with one from another gauge cluster, and everything has worked OK since.<P>Recently the speedometer started acting up again.  I found that the wire from the VSS had rubbed against the passenger side axle and rubbed the insulation off the wires.  I was able to play with the wires to get it working until I have time to buy another connector and splice it into the wiring harness.<P>If the car has sat for a long time, there are a lot of connections between the VSS and the speedometer that could be bad or corroded.  You might want to try reseating the VSS connector and the 2 wiring harness connections to the instrument panel.  Perhaps a little contact cleaner would help.<P>The good news is that spare speedometers are easily availabel for the 85mph units.  Some are even available in junkyards here in NC (where almost no Fieros went to die).<BR><P>------------------<BR>Bob<BR>2 - 87 GT's<BR>85 SE 4 cyl||||reg||1
Z||000006||MooCow||12-09-2000||08:51 AM||||The needle is stuck at 35.  It never moves at all.  The car ran so good.  Now if only my truck would sell I would be good.<P>                              Thanks Ken||||reg||1
